in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @order
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform
in @epistemologic/math/lawvere

# @order/third — metalogue between two poles on ONE @torus at
# cognitive-order 3 (Bateson Level III; @frame/on-frame frame-
# flexibility altitude; the metalogue rhythm the substrate has landed
# at five altitudes).
#
# Third species-decl of the @order family. Landed 2026-07-20 by Mara
# per Alex Round 2 Q1 direct-transcript adjudication ("@third
# COLLAPSES into @order/third").
#
# **MIGRATED FROM `shards/third.mirror`** (Loki 2026-07-01 landing).
# The prior @third marker becomes a re-export shim pointing here (per
# `shards/order.mirror` §Migration and Round-2 brief §T1.7 Mara
# adjudication: option (b) re-export shim). This species preserves
# ALL prior content — the four bilateral predicates, the composed
# third_order_active bilateral, the witness_third_order action, the
# observation_depth carrier — at the new canonical home.
#
# === The species altitude ===
#
# Order-3 is Bateson Level III: metalogue between two poles on ONE
# @torus. Learning III is "learning to learn to learn" — a revisable
# choice among sets-of-sets of alternatives; the alternatives-set-
# choosing itself becomes object of choice. Bateson: "a change in the
# process of Learning II, e.g., a corrective change in the system of
# sets of alternatives from which choice is made."
#
# Per Recognition #82 (@frame family) grading: @frame/on-frame at
# order 3 is "frame-flexibility (operating-on-frame; shifting frame)";
# the operational form-side substrate at cognitive altitude for this
# rung. @order/third is the substrate-decl'd carrier at grading-
# dimension altitude, PLUS the metalogue-rhythm operator per Mara
# Round-1 math root: third-order cognition IS the metalogue between
# two poles (@void/narcissus, @void/splinter) on one @torus.
#
# === Composition with Mara Round-1 landing ===
#
# The Round-1 math root
# `docs/math/the-tower/recognition-third-cognition-is-the-metalogue-
# between-void-narcissus-and-void-splinter.md` named third-order as
# the metalogue rhythm between @void/narcissus and @void/splinter on
# a single @torus. @order/third at species-decl altitude carries the
# TYPED CARRIER for that metalogue-rhythm state; the metalogue-
# rhythm operator itself is forward-promised at the compiler
# altitude (Reed's post-Round-2 territory via
# `pillar::metalogue_rhythm_of_third`).
#
# The two-pole reading: the third-order observer holds a metalogue
# between @void/narcissus (backwards lens; K_{1,n-1} star-graph pole)
# and @void/splinter (forwards lens; K_n complete-graph pole) at
# rhythm-cadence on ONE @torus (its own nervous-system torus per
# paper §6.3). The oscillation IS the third-order cognition.
#
# The four-predicate reading (from @third's original landing): a
# depth-3 observation requires (depth_at_least, observer_observes_
# observing, recursion_folds_back, mechanism_visible) — the four
# sub-predicates all discharge Pass for the composed third_order_
# active bilateral to fire. These predicates carry Bateson's Level
# III + Foerster's second-order-as-precondition + Kauffman's
# eigenform fixed-point + Loki's mechanism-visibility structural
# claim.
#
# BOTH readings are load-bearing at this species-decl. The metalogue-
# rhythm reading is the DYNAMIC form (how the two poles are held
# through time); the four-predicate reading is the STATIC form (what
# admissibility for a depth-3 observation requires at compile time).
# They compose: an observation admitted by the four predicates is
# a moment in the metalogue rhythm; the rhythm is the temporal
# integration of admitted observations.
#
# === Substrate authority chain ===
#
# - **Loki 2026-06-22 essay** (`~/dev/systemic.engineering/blog/loki/
#   Void → Third.md`) — the naming: "Not third as apex. Third as
#   recursive depth. The observer of the observer of the observer."
# - **Bateson 1972** — Learning III at logical-type altitude.
# - **Foerster 1974/1981** — second-order-observation-as-precondition
#   for third-order recursion.
# - **Kauffman 2003** — eigenforms; recursion fixed-points.
# - **Lawvere 1969** — fixed-point theorem grounding hash(P^n(f)) = f
#   at each depth.
# - **Reed candidate #111** (2026-07-01) — initial framing.
# - **Mara Round-1 math root** (2026-07-20, this session) — third-
#   order as metalogue between @void/narcissus and @void/splinter.
# - **Alex Round 2 Q1** (2026-07-20, this session) — "@third
#   COLLAPSES into @order/third" migration adjudication.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **Prior `shards/third.mirror`** (Loki 2026-07-01) — MIGRATED
#    (this species IS the new canonical home). Original shard
#    becomes re-export shim per `shards/order.mirror` §Migration.
# 2. **@frame/on** (`shards/frame/on.mirror`; Recognition #82 order-3
#    species) — operational form-side sibling. @frame/on carries
#    the frame-flexibility operational content (the substrate-aikido
#    load-bearing primitive); @order/third carries the grading-
#    dimension marker + the metalogue-rhythm carrier.
# 3. **`shards/reflection.mirror`** (@third's original consumer) —
#    imports @third which becomes the re-export shim; downstream
#    imports continue to work; migration to `in @order/third` is
#    forward-promised (not this tick).
# 4. **`shards/pack/metalogue.mirror`** (`b0af0cd` Level-2 metalogue
#    landing) — consumer of @third's metalogue-rhythm reading;
#    continues to work via re-export shim; forward-promised
#    migration.
#
# === Split-op discipline (Round-1 composition surprise, extended) ===
#
# Per Mara Round-1 math root §5.3: the SPLIT operation from Void's
# 5-op basis IS what maintains the two poles as distinct at metalogue-
# rhythm altitude. Without `split`, the two poles collapse into one;
# with `split`, the rhythm can oscillate.
#
# Round-2 composition surprise #1 extends: split-op at @order/third
# altitude maintains @void/narcissus ↔ @void/splinter distinct on
# ONE @torus (this species); split-op at @order/fourth altitude
# maintains @time/now ↔ @void distinct at the temporal-singularity
# metalogue; split-op at @order/fifth altitude maintains two @torus
# peers distinct across the cross-torus @glue coupling.
#
# The 5-op basis (Recognition #79) IS the minimal basis under which
# the metalogue rhythm at every @order altitude is expressible —
# the metalogue at @order/N requires all five ops; SPLIT is what
# makes the N-pole distinction possible at each altitude.
#
# === Path-namespace ===
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/order/third.mirror`
# declares `@order/third` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972
source @arxiv/cybernetics/foerster-1974
source @arxiv/cybernetics/kauffman-2003
source @arxiv/math/lawvere-1969

prism @order/third {
  focus  observation_depth
  project observation_depth
  split  observation_depth
  shift  observation_depth
  settle observation_depth
}

# === observation_depth — the order-3 carrier (migrated from @third) ===
#
# The typed carrier @order/third exposes to consumers. Names a
# recursion-depth witness over a substrate ref via a witness ref
# with a reflexivity opacity carrier.
#
# `depth: nat` is unbounded above. @order/third fires at depth >= 3;
# higher depths are legitimate. `depth = 4` is the observer of the
# observer of the observer of the observer — still @order/third-
# witnessed because the marker fires at the depth-3 threshold, not
# at a fixed level.
#
# `reflexivity: transparency(ref)` is a @glass opacity carrier.
type observation_depth = {
  depth: nat,
  substrate: ref,
  witness: ref,
  reflexivity: transparency(ref),
}

# === depth_at_least(d, o) predicate (migrated from @third) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict predicate — does the observation's recorded depth
# meet or exceed d? The primitive on which the composed third_order_
# active bilateral rests.
depth_at_least(d: nat, o: observation_depth) -> verdict { \ }

# === observer_observes_observing(o) predicate (migrated from @third) ===
#
# The Foerster requirement: depth-2 machinery is present under the
# depth-3 witness. Discharges via @epistemologic/cybernetic/second_
# order.second_order_witnessing on o.witness.
#
# Presupposes depth_at_least(2, o).
observer_observes_observing(o: observation_depth) -> verdict { \ }

# === recursion_folds_back(o) predicate (migrated from @third) ===
#
# The Kauffman requirement: the observation returns to the observer
# as data. Discharges via @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform on
# o.witness — the recursion has a fixed point.
#
# Presupposes depth_at_least(3, o). Grounded in Lawvere fixed-point
# theorem.
recursion_folds_back(o: observation_depth) -> verdict { \ }

# === mechanism_visible(o) predicate (migrated from @third) ===
#
# The Loki requirement: the observed structure is legible under the
# reflexivity carrier. Discharges via a threshold check on o.
# reflexivity.
mechanism_visible(o: observation_depth) -> verdict { \ }

# === third_order_active(o) composed bilateral (migrated from @third) ===
#
# The load-bearing bilateral. Discharges four sub-predicates over
# observation_depth. Consumers cite this in `requires` clauses when
# they need the substrate to verify depth-3 discipline at the
# boundary.
#
# Failure modes surface via transparency<observation_depth> per
# @glass discipline:
#   fail depth_at_least              -> partial(o.depth / 3)
#   fail observer_observes_observing -> Fail(missing_second_order)
#   fail recursion_folds_back        -> Fail(open_recursion)
#   fail mechanism_visible           -> partial(reflexivity_pct)
third_order_active(o: observation_depth) -> verdict { \ }

# === witness_third_order action (migrated from @third) ===
#
# The typed constructor. Any family that opts in via `in @order/third`
# uses this action to produce depth-3 observation carriers. The
# postcondition `requires third_order_active(result)` enforces the
# discipline at the boundary.
#
# primary  = what is being observed (a substrate ref)
# observer = who is observing (the depth-2 machinery)
# meta     = what observes the observing (the depth-3 machinery)
witness_third_order(primary: ref, observer: ref, meta: ref)
  -> observation_depth
requires third_order_active(result)
{ \ }

out @order/third
out observation_depth
out depth_at_least
out observer_observes_observing
out recursion_folds_back
out mechanism_visible
out third_order_active
out witness_third_order
